## Detailed Design

### Step 1: Expand & Sync (Pre-Deploy Job before v2.1)
```sql
SET SESSION lock_wait_timeout = 2;
ALTER TABLE customers ADD COLUMN phone_e164 VARCHAR(20) NULL, ALGORITHM=INSTANT;

CREATE TRIGGER trg_customers_ins BEFORE INSERT ON customers
FOR EACH ROW BEGIN
  IF NEW.phone_e164 IS NULL THEN SET NEW.phone_e164 = NEW.user_phone; END IF;
  IF NEW.user_phone IS NULL THEN SET NEW.user_phone = NEW.phone_e164; END IF;
END;

CREATE TRIGGER trg_customers_upd BEFORE UPDATE ON customers
FOR EACH ROW BEGIN
  IF NEW.phone_e164 <=> OLD.phone_e164 AND NOT (NEW.user_phone <=> OLD.user_phone) THEN
    SET NEW.phone_e164 = NEW.user_phone;
  ELSIF NEW.user_phone <=> OLD.user_phone AND NOT (NEW.phone_e164 <=> OLD.phone_e164) THEN
    SET NEW.user_phone = NEW.phone_e164;
  END IF;
END;
```

### Step 2: Throttled Backfill & Online Index
Backfill `phone_e164 = user_phone` in 2,000-row `WHERE id > ? ORDER BY id LIMIT 2000` batches (checking `Threads_running` and replica lag). Then create the index online:
```sql
ALTER TABLE customers ADD INDEX idx_phone_e164 (phone_e164), ALGORITHM=INPLACE, LOCK=NONE;
```

### Step 3: Deploy v2.1 & Contract in v2.2
Deploy v2.1 reading/writing `phone_e164` (with `COALESCE(phone_e164, user_phone)` as a defensive fallback). Once v2.0 is fully retired and rollback is no longer needed, deploy v2.2's Contract migration:
```sql
DROP TRIGGER trg_customers_ins;
DROP TRIGGER trg_customers_upd;
ALTER TABLE customers DROP COLUMN user_phone, ALGORITHM=INSTANT;
```
